 },
 "critic": "The cards read as templates because names, occupations, locations and rewards occupy interchangeable slots, while individual relationships and motives receive little detail. Repeated full names and phrases such as 'no questions' reinforce that impression. Exact duplicates and recurring fee, accident, theft and delivery structures repeat across the set. The Friday collection feels most caused because an established gang practice creates a specific financial pressure. Repairs and debt collection also connect a problem to a practical response. Sealed deliveries and surveillance assignments give clear instructions but little reason for the underlying situation. Ambient incidents sometimes suggest a living street, yet often leave no meaningful lead. Identical pair texts required arbitrary choices."
